cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "PILAR-2b: Plataforma Inteligente de Localização e Aproveitamento de Resíduos para Biogas e Bioprodutos"
version: "3.0.3"
date-released: "2026-05-18"
license: GPL-3.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/aikiesan/Pilar-2b"
url: "https://cp2b.unicamp.br/pilar2b/pt-BR"
abstract: >
  PILAR-2b is an open-source microservices platform for analyzing biogas and
  bioproduct potential from agricultural, livestock, and urban residues across
  645 municipalities in São Paulo State, Brazil. It integrates heterogeneous
  government datasets (IBGE, MapBiomas, ABIOVE) into a unified geospatial
  database with a browser-based interface that requires no desktop GIS software.
  The platform implements a feedstock-dependent correction factor (FDE)
  methodology that decomposes theoretical biomass potential into practical
  mobilisable availability, and quantifies the spatial distribution of biogas
  potential at municipal resolution within an open and replicable computational
  architecture.
keywords:
